I've been talking to a YC founder who's 15 years in and still doing big new things. One of the biggest popular misconceptions about startups is that founders have a brilliant idea, then implement it. In fact more often than not the biggest idea comes later.

The mistaken belief that everything depends on the initial idea hoses you in multiple ways. It makes you give up if the initial idea doesn't work. But it also puts too much weight on it: if everything depends on the initial idea, it has to be huge.

